# Benchmark fixture corpus.  test/ is ~3.9 GB of CHIFFON libraries, HGC/BRCH
# tables and recorded .out/.sum baselines distributed out of band; the
# consolidated snapshot excludes it for the same reason.  Only C++ contract
# tests that live beside the fixtures -- and the frozen validation reference
# manifests, which are a few KB of JSON and ARE the campaign's acceptance
# contract -- are tracked.  The directory itself has to be re-included first:
# git does not descend into an ignored directory to find a negated file.
/test/**
!/test/*.cpp
!/test/*.h
# .cu belongs here for the same reason .cpp does.  Without it every device test
# had to be `git add -f`'d, and one of them -- test/nodal_mine_device.cu, the
# miner behind NODAL_FORMS in src/NodalKernel.h -- was simply forgotten, leaving
# CMakeLists.txt naming a source no clone had.  That took the whole
# RASBERY_ENABLE_TESTS=ON configure down until Task 5 guarded it.  This line is
# the cause; the guard was the symptom.
!/test/*.cu
!/test/.gitignore
!/test/reference/
!/test/reference/*.json

# Local scratch left by review passes (not an artifact of the build).
/.cleanup_findings.txt
